id-market rents in Austin, Texas, fell by <strong data-note=\"9\">11 percent<\/strong> between September 2022 and September 2025, reversing over one-third of the 29 percent increase in the two years before that."]}, {"type": "prose", "heading": "Building Alone Won’t Solve Housing Affordability Crisis", "paragraphs": ["Expanding supply alone, however, can’t solve the housing affordability crisis. It will rarely reduce housing costs to levels that are affordable to people with incomes around or below the poverty line, who are by far the most likely to struggle to afford housing."]}, {"type": "scrolly", "figure": {"number": 1, "title": "Most Severely Cost-Burdened Renters Have Extremely Low Incomes", "subtitle": "Share of renters paying more than half their income for housing, by HUD income category; 1 box = 1%", "source": "Source: CBPP analysis of 2024 American Community Survey data and 2024 HUD income limits", "chart": {"type": "waffle", "cols": 10, "total": 100, "format": "pct", "valueLabel": "Share of severely cost-burdened renters", "alt": "Waffle chart of 100 boxes: 70 are extremely low income, 21 very low income, 7 low income and 2 middle income.", "categories": [{"key": "eli", "label": "Extremely low income", "desc": "Up to poverty line or 30% AMI", "value": 70, "color": "#f0626b"}, {"key": "vli", "label": "Very low income", "desc": "Above extremely low, up to 50% AMI", "value": 21, "color": "#ffdfa3"}, {"key": "li", "label": "Low income", "desc": "51–80% AMI", "value": 7, "color": "#d3c9bf"}, {"key": "mid", "label": "Middle income", "desc": "> 80% area median income (AMI)", "value": 2, "color": "#9b9b9b"}]}}, "steps": [{"html": "<p>In 2024, <strong data-note=\"15\" data-guess=\"no endnote on this sentence; the next sentence’s endnote (CBPP analysis of American Community Survey data) covers the same analysis\">25 million people<\/strong> lived in households that paid more than 50 percent of their income for rent, far above the 30 percent of income that is consi